#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.11"
# dependencies = ["pyyaml"]
# ///
"""BOSH Acceptance Tests (BATS) runner against the configured PVE lab.

Drives the upstream cloudfoundry/bosh-acceptance-tests rspec suite against
the live BOSH director this repo's e2e harness stands up, using the same env
bundles, config file, and secret sources. It resolves the checkout, patches
in the PVE cloud-config template (manifests/bats/cloud_config_pve.yml.erb),
renders bat.yml from the active env bundle, runs rspec with the PVE tag
exclusions, restores the director's cloud config afterward, and writes both
machine artifacts (.e2e-results/<ts>/) and the committed proof documents
(docs/certification/bats/runs/<date>-<hhmmss>.md plus the README.md summary).

Usage:
    ./scripts/bats [command] [flags]

Commands:
    run          (default) preflight -> prepare -> rspec -> finalize.
                 Requires a running director (see scripts/e2e bootstrap).
    report       Re-print the summary table from the most recent run.
    help         Show this message.

Flags:
    --config FILE       Integration config YAML (default: ci/integration.yml).
    --env NAME          BOSH_PVE_ENV overlay selector (default: $BOSH_PVE_ENV
                        or 'cpitest').
    --stemcell WHAT     'light' (default) builds/reuses the light stemcell the
                        env already uses, or a path to a stemcell .tgz.
    --exclude TAG       Extra rspec tag to exclude, repeatable. Adds to the
                        built-in PVE exclusion set.
    --no-default-excludes
                        Drop the built-in PVE exclusion set (run everything
                        except --exclude tags).
    --only TAG          Run only examples with this tag, repeatable. Naming a
                        dual-stack tag (ipv6, dual_stack) switches the run to
                        the dual-stack pass, which deploys a job on both the
                        IPv4 and the IPv6 network. That pass is opt-in: the
                        agent cannot hold two static addresses on one NIC yet,
                        so a default run leaves it out.
    --fail-fast         Stop rspec at the first failure.
    --keep              Set BAT_DEBUG_MODE: fail fast and leave the failed
                        deployment, stemcell, and release in place.
    --results-dir DIR   Where to write artifacts (default: .e2e-results).
    --skip-doc          Do not write docs/certification/bats/ report documents.
    --headline-pass-fail-only
                        Regenerate the README "Latest run" headline only from
                        runs with a definite PASS/FAIL verdict; an UNKNOWN run
                        still commits its run document but leaves the headline
                        on the last decisive run. Scheduled CI runs pass this.
    --dry-run           Print every command without executing; exit 0.
    --no-color          Disable ANSI color.

Env:
    BOSH_PVE_ENV        Env bundle selector (see manifests/envs/).
    BATS_DIR            Existing bosh-acceptance-tests checkout to use instead
                        of the managed .deps/ clone.
    STEMCELL_PATH       Fallback stemcell tarball when --stemcell is a 'light'
                        run and no light stemcell can be built.

Exit codes:
    0    all steps passed
    1    a step failed (including rspec failures)
    2    ruby or bundler not installed (soft skip), or usage error
    124  a step hit its timeout
    130  interrupted
"""

